# Citation metadata for this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
#
# Validated against the CFF 1.2.0 JSON schema. Only four top-level keys are required
# (cff-version, message, title, authors); everything else below is optional.
#
# Four keys are DELIBERATELY OMITTED rather than filled with a placeholder, because a
# placeholder here is either schema-invalid or -- worse -- silently accepted as if it
# were true, and then propagates into BibTeX/APA/Zenodo metadata as a dead link or a
# DOI that does not resolve:
#
#   license:         must be an SPDX identifier from the CFF 1.2.0 enumeration. A
#                    free-text value such as "proprietary" or "LicenseRef-..." is
#                    REJECTED by the schema; there is no escape hatch in CFF 1.2.0.
#                    The authors have not yet chosen a licence (see LICENSE_PENDING.txt),
#                    so the key is omitted. Add `license: MIT` (or the chosen SPDX id)
#                    once the licence is settled.
#   date-released:   must match ^[0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[012])-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])$.
#                    Add it only with the real release date.
#   repository-code: the real https:// URL of the public source repository. Add it once
#                    the repository has been created.
#   identifiers:     the real Zenodo DOI, as a BARE value of the form
#                    10.5281/zenodo.NNNNNNN -- no https://doi.org/ prefix. Add it only
#                    after Zenodo has issued the DOI for the archived release. A DOI is
#                    not invented here.
#
# When the DOI exists, the block to add back is:
#
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: 10.5281/zenodo.<NNNNNNN>
#       description: "Zenodo archive of version 1.1.0"
#
